# Where the contact and volunteer forms deliver.
#
# The site is a static export, so there is no server of our own to receive a
# POST and nowhere safe to hold an SMTP credential. Both forms send a JSON body
# to this endpoint instead; any form-to-email service that accepts JSON works —
# Formspree, Web3Forms, Basin, Netlify Forms.
#
# Leave it unset and the forms do not pretend to work: each renders a short
# notice and the association's email address instead.
#
# The value is public by design (it ships in the client bundle), so use an
# endpoint that is safe to expose and has the provider's own spam filtering on.
# Ours adds a honeypot field on top of it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FORM_ENDPOINT=
